{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTransposeBridge","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelDimPos","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Slope"],"declarations":111,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_nonpos_of_FMP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_nonpos_of_FMP","kind":"theorem","line":1607,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1607-L1612","doc":"**FMP ⇒ leg [A2] (machine-checked)**: fractional-moment positivity near the boundary forces\n`Cov₂(ln f, ω₃) ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.FractionalMomentPositivity.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.FractionalMomentPositivity.pos","kind":"theorem","line":1605,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1605-L1605","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.FractionalMomentPositivity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.FractionalMomentPositivity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1604,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1604-L1604","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.FractionalMomentPositivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.FractionalMomentPositivity","kind":"class","line":1598,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1598-L1605","doc":"**Fractional-moment positivity (FMP)** — the new instance-less target *above* leg [A2]: the\nfamily `M_α` is nonnegative on some right neighborhood of the boundary. Exact-`Fraction` verified\n`n ≤ 30` on `α ∈ [0.02, 6]` (with the minimum always at the [A2] boundary `α → 0⁺` and survival\npast the `n ≥ 29` pointwise falsification — the failing bounded weights lie outside the power\nfamily). Providing this instance for all `k` closes leg [A2] via the bridge below. NO instance is\nprovided — that is the open problem, one level sharper than [A2] itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nu_log_nonneg_of_fracMoment_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nu_log_nonneg_of_fracMoment_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":1581,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1581-L1596","doc":"**The FMP ⇒ [A2] bridge**: if the fractional-moment family is nonnegative on any right\nneighborhood `(0, ε)` of the boundary, the log moment is nonnegative — `0 = M(0) ≤ M(α)` near `0`\nforces the one-sided derivative, which IS the [A2] quantity, to be `≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_fracMoment_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_fracMoment_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1559,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1559-L1579","doc":"**`M′(0) = Σ ln(v)·ν_v`** — the fractional-moment family's derivative at the boundary is\nexactly the [A2] log moment (term-by-term `exp` differentiation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.fracMoment_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.fracMoment_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1553,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1553-L1557","doc":"`M(0) = Σ_v ν_v = 0` — the zeroth-moment constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.fracMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.fracMoment","kind":"def","line":1547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1547-L1551","doc":"**The fractional-moment family** `M_α = Σ_v v^α·ν_v`, in `exp(α·ln v)` form (the `v = 0` term\nis the constant `exp(α·ln 0) = exp(0) = 1` under Lean's `Real.log 0 = 0`, and is annihilated by\n`nuV_zero`, so the convention is harmless). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuV_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuV_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1532-L1545","doc":"The ν-system vanishes at `v = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1526-L1530","doc":"No hooks of length zero: the `v = 0` fiber of the spectrum is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_nonpos_iff_nu_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_nonpos_iff_nu_log","kind":"theorem","line":1507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1507-L1513","doc":"**Leg [A2] in pure ν-form (capstone)**: `Cov₂(ln f, ω₃) ≤ 0 ↔ Σ_v ln(v)·ν_v ≥ 0`. The open\nkernel leg is exactly: *the mean-zero (`sum_nuV_eq_zero`), positive-second-moment\n(`sum_sq_nuV_nonneg`) signed measure `ν` has nonnegative log moment.* ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_log_nuV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_log_nuV","kind":"theorem","line":1499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1499-L1505","doc":"**The ν-system's log moment is the [A2] hook covariance**:\n`Σ_v ln(v)·ν_v = Cov₂(ln ∏h, ω₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_sq_nuV_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_sq_nuV_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":1493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1493-L1497","doc":"`Σ_v v²·ν_v ≥ 0` — the positive-second-moment constraint in pure ν-form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_sq_nuV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_sq_nuV","kind":"theorem","line":1485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1485-L1491","doc":"**The ν-system's second moment is the proved variance**:\n`Σ_v v²·ν_v = Cov₂(Σh², ω₃) (= Var₂(ω₃))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_weighted_nuV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_weighted_nuV","kind":"theorem","line":1435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1435-L1483","doc":"**Weighted ν-sums are statistic covariances**: for every weight `φ`,\n`Σ_v φ(v)·ν_v = Cov₂(Σ_v φ(v)·N_v, ω₃)` — covariance is linear in the statistic, and the\n`v`-sum assembles the diagram statistic `Σ_v φ(v)·N_v(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covStat_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covStat_congr","kind":"theorem","line":1425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1425-L1433","doc":"`covStat` respects member-wise equality of statistics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covStat","kind":"def","line":1418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1418-L1423","doc":"Generic diagram-statistic covariance `Cov₂(S, ω₃)` (the shape shared by `covHookSq`,\n`covLnHooks`, and the ν-moment sums). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.spectral_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.spectral_log","kind":"theorem","line":1410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1410-L1416","doc":"Spectral instance `φ = ln`: `Σ_v ln(v)·N_v = ln ∏h` per diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.spectral_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.spectral_sq","kind":"theorem","line":1400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1400-L1408","doc":"Spectral instance `φ = (·)²`: `Σ_v v²·N_v = Σ_□h²` per diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.log_hookProd_eq_sum_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.log_hookProd_eq_sum_cells","kind":"theorem","line":1391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1391-L1398","doc":"`ln ∏h` as a cell-set sum of hook logs (`hookProd_eq_prod_cells` + `Real.log_prod`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sumSqHooks_eq_sum_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sumSqHooks_eq_sum_cells","kind":"theorem","line":1359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1359-L1389","doc":"`IdentityI.sumSqHooks` as a cell-set sum of the kernel-form hook (the two per-cell\nℕ-subtraction forms agree on genuine cells, as in `hookProd_eq_prodHooks`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.six_mul_omega3_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.six_mul_omega3_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":1310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1310-L1357","doc":"**The bracket-arithmetic hinge**: on the hook shape with arm `a = i+1` and leg `c = k−1−i`,\nsix times the 3-cycle eigenvalue is the quadratic the collapse consumes,\n\n`6·ω₃ = 2k·(3i² − 3(k−1)i + (k−1)(k−2))`.\n\nThe cubic terms of the arm and leg content sums cancel identically — this is the cancellation\nrecorded in `BinomialSquareSums`, here proved at the level of the diagram data\n(`contentSq_hookShape` + `six_mul_sum_range_sq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.two_mul_choose_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.two_mul_choose_two","kind":"theorem","line":1301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1301-L1308","doc":"`2·C(k,2) = k(k−1)` — the `ℕ`-division in `omega3`'s centre term is exact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_range_succ_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_range_succ_shift","kind":"theorem","line":1295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1295-L1299","doc":"Index shift for the column contents: `Σ_{t<c} (t+1)² = Σ_{j<c+1} j²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.top_mixedMoment_eq_hookShapes_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.top_mixedMoment_eq_hookShapes_sum","kind":"theorem","line":1275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1275-L1293","doc":"**The top mixed moment restricts to the hook shapes.** Combining the carrier confinement\n(`N_k = 1` on hook shapes, `0` elsewhere) with the enumeration transfer: the `v = k` numerator of\nthe ν-system is a sum over the `k` hook shapes alone. This is the wiring step that turns the\nper-diagram carrier lemma into the classical single-index sum of the (TAIL) first instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_top_eq_one_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_top_eq_one_mem","kind":"theorem","line":1254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1254-L1273","doc":"The top hook statistic is `1` on every enumerated hook shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_top_eq_zero_of_not_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_top_eq_zero_of_not_mem","kind":"theorem","line":1244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1244-L1252","doc":"The top hook statistic vanishes off the hook shapes, *as members of the enumerator*: the\n`getD`-level carrier lemma transported to the enumeration via `mem_hookShapes_of_rows_le_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_partsOf_eq_sum_hookShapes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_partsOf_eq_sum_hookShapes","kind":"theorem","line":1225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1225-L1242","doc":"**Step 3 (the Plancherel restriction)**: a weight vanishing off the hook shapes may be summed\nover the explicit `k`-element family `hookShapes k` instead of the whole enumerator `partsOf k`.\nBoth lists are nodup (`partsFuel_nodup`, `hookShapes_nodup`) and the family embeds\n(`hookShape_mem_partsOf`), so this is `Finset.sum_subset` transported along `List.sum_toFinset`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sytDim_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sytDim_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":1205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1205-L1223","doc":"**SYT dimension of a hook shape**: `f^{(a,1^c)} = C(n−1, a−1)` with `n = a + c` — the\nhook-length formula evaluated on the hook-shape data. Step 2 of the (TAIL) first-instance\nderivation, feeding the binomial-square sums. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.mem_hookShapes_of_rows_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.mem_hookShapes_of_rows_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":1177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1177-L1203","doc":"A hook-shaped member of `partsOf k` is in the enumeration `hookShapes k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.eq_hookShape_of_rows_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.eq_hookShape_of_rows_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":1156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1156-L1175","doc":"**Converse structural fact**: a nonempty list all of whose rows past the first are `≤ 1`, with\npositive entries, *is* the hook shape `(head, 1^{len−1})`. Together with the carrier lemma this\nmakes \"is a hook shape\" (a `getD` condition) and \"belongs to `hookShapes`\" (an enumeration\ncondition) interchangeable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShapes_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShapes_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":1148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1148-L1154","doc":"The hook-shape enumeration has no duplicates (the arm length is the head). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShape_mem_partsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShape_mem_partsOf","kind":"theorem","line":1133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1133-L1146","doc":"Every hook shape is a genuine member of the partition enumerator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShape_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShape_sum","kind":"theorem","line":1127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1127-L1131","doc":"Each enumerated hook shape has size `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShapes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShapes","kind":"def","line":1123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1123-L1125","doc":"The `k` hook shapes of size `k`, enumerated by arm length `a = i + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookProd_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookProd_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":1054,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1054-L1113","doc":"**Hook product of a hook shape** `(a, 1^c)`: the corner hook is `a + c = n`, the arm hooks\ndescend `a−1, …, 1`, the leg hooks descend `c, …, 1` — so `∏h = n·(a−1)!·c!`. Step 2 of the\n(TAIL) first-instance derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookProd_eq_finset_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookProd_eq_finset_prod","kind":"theorem","line":1046,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1046-L1052","doc":"`hookProd` as a nested `Finset.range` product (row-structured form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.prod_range_sub_eq_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.prod_range_sub_eq_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":1035,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1035-L1044","doc":"Descending-factor product: `∏_{j<m} (m − j) = m!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_replicate_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_replicate_one","kind":"theorem","line":1026,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1026-L1033","doc":"The size of a hook shape is `a + c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sorted_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sorted_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":1015,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1015-L1024","doc":"Hook shapes are weakly decreasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.six_mul_sum_range_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.six_mul_sum_range_sq","kind":"theorem","line":1003,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L1003-L1013","doc":"Division-free sum of squares: `6·Σ_{j<m} j² = (m−1)·m·(2m−1)` in `ℤ` — the polynomial\nevaluation of the hook-shape content data (`Q(m) = Σ_{t≤m} t²` in the audit's notation is\n`Σ_{j<m+1} j²` here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.contentSq_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.contentSq_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":982,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L982-L1001","doc":"**Content square of a hook shape** `(a, 1^c)`: row 0 contributes the squares of the arm\ncontents `0, …, a−1`; the column cells `(i,0)`, `1 ≤ i ≤ c`, contribute `(−i)² = i²`. This is\nstep 2 of the (TAIL) first-instance derivation (`ω₃ = Q(a−1) + Q(c) − C(n,2)` after subtracting\nthe center term). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.getD_replicate_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.getD_replicate_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":969,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L969-L980","doc":"`getD` on a replicate list, in range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_sum_of_not_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_sum_of_not_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":957,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L957-L967","doc":"**Carrier confinement, count form (non-hook shape)**: off the hook shapes the top hook\nstatistic vanishes, `N_n = 0` — a cell of hook length `n` would force the hook shape by the\ncarrier lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_sum_of_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount_sum_of_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":932,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L932-L955","doc":"**Carrier confinement, count form (hook shape)**: on a hook shape the top hook statistic is\nexactly `N_n = 1` — the corner is the *unique* cell of hook length `n` (existence by\n`hookLen_corner_of_hookShape`, uniqueness by the carrier lemma\n`hookShape_of_hookLen_eq_sum`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_corner_of_hookShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_corner_of_hookShape","kind":"theorem","line":896,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L896-L930","doc":"**Converse of the carrier lemma**: on a hook shape (positive parts, at most one cell per row\npast the first) the corner's hook exhausts the diagram — `h(0,0) = a + λ′₀ − 1 = a + c = n`.\nTogether with `hookShape_of_hookLen_eq_sum` this characterizes the carriers of the top hook\nstatistic `N_n`: they are exactly the corner cells of the `n` hook shapes `(a, 1^{n−a})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShape_of_hookLen_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookShape_of_hookLen_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":807,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L807-L894","doc":"**The carrier lemma (equality analysis)**: a hook of maximal length `n = Σλᵢ` forces the\ncarrier cell to be the corner `(0,0)` and the diagram to be a **hook shape** (every row past the\nfirst has at most one cell, i.e. `λ = (a, 1^c)`). Equality in `hookLen_le_sum`'s containment\nmeans the arm ∪ strict-leg union *is* the cell set; testing the corner against the union pins\n`p = (0,0)`, and testing any cell `(i′,1)` with `i′ ≥ 1` (off row 0 and column 0) kills any\nnon-hook row. This confines the carriers of the top hook statistic `N_n` to the `n` hook shapes\n— the Lean form of step 1 of the derived `ν_n` closed form (the (TAIL) first instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_le_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_le_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":800,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L800-L805","doc":"The tight hook bound on enumerated partitions: `h(□) ≤ k` (sharpening the cheap `2k`\nrange bound `hookLen_lt_of_mem`; the classical bound, now proved rather than assumed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_le_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_le_sum","kind":"theorem","line":753,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L753-L798","doc":"**The hook is contained in the diagram**: a cell's hook length is at most the size\n`n = Σλᵢ`. The hook of `(i,j)` is the disjoint union of its arm `{(i,j′) : j ≤ j′ < λᵢ}` and\nits strict leg `{(i′,j) : i < i′ < λ′ⱼ}`, both inside the cell set; counting the union gives\n`h(i,j) = (λᵢ − j) + (λ′ⱼ − i − 1) ≤ |cells λ| = n`. This is the first brick of the (TAIL)\ncarrier method: the extreme case `h = n` forces the hook to *exhaust* the diagram, confining\nthe carriers of `ν_n` to the hook shapes `(a, 1^{n−a})` — the containment proved here is the\ninequality whose equality analysis is that carrier lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_pos","kind":"theorem","line":743,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L743-L751","doc":"Hooks are positive on genuine cells (cell bound + its staircase mirror). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_nuV_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_nuV_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":692,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L692-L734","doc":"**The zeroth-moment constraint, Lean-locked**: `Σ_v ν_v = 0` — the spectrum totals to the\nconstant `k`, and covariance against a constant vanishes. Together with the second moment\n(`Σ_v v²·ν_v = Var₂(ω₃) ≥ 0`, via `covHookSq_nonneg`) and the [A2] target\n(`Σ_v ln(v)·ν_v ≥ 0 ⇔` leg [A2], via `covLnF_nonpos_iff`), this pins the surviving moment\nskeleton's exact shape: a mean-zero signed measure with positive second moment whose log-moment\nsign is the open leg. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_hookCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sum_hookCount","kind":"theorem","line":683,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L683-L690","doc":"The spectrum totals to the size: `Σ_v N_v(λ) = k` (φ = 1 in the spectral decomposition,\nplus `|cells| = k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.finset_sum_list_map_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.finset_sum_list_map_sum","kind":"theorem","line":675,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L675-L681","doc":"A `Finset`-indexed family of list sums swaps with the list sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuV","kind":"def","line":671,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L671-L673","doc":"**The ν-system**: `ν_v = Cov₂(N_v, ω₃)` — the hook-spectrum/content-spread covariances whose\nlog-moment sign is leg [A2]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuMean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuMean","kind":"def","line":667,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L667-L669","doc":"Spectrum mean `E₂[N_v]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuMixedMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.nuMixedMoment","kind":"def","line":662,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L662-L665","doc":"Mixed spectrum moment `E₂[N_v·ω₃]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookSpectrum_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookSpectrum_sum","kind":"theorem","line":643,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L643-L660","doc":"**The spectral decomposition of hook statistics**: for every `φ`,\n`Σ_v φ(v)·N_v(λ) = Σ_□ φ(h(□))` — fiberwise summation of the cell set over hook values. This is\nthe exact mechanism by which the ν-system's moments realize the scaffold's hook covariances\n(`φ = ln` ↦ `covLnHooks`, `φ = (·)²` ↦ `covHookSq`, `φ = 1` ↦ the zeroth moment below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_lt_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen_lt_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":632,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L632-L641","doc":"The cheap hook bound on enumerated partitions: `h(□) ≤ λ_i + λ'_j ≤ 2k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.getD_le_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.getD_le_sum","kind":"theorem","line":619,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L619-L630","doc":"Any single part is at most the size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookCount","kind":"def","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L615-L617","doc":"**The hook spectrum** `N_v(λ)`: the number of cells with hook length `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookLen","kind":"def","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L611-L613","doc":"The hook length of a cell, in the kernel's per-cell form `λ_i + λ'_j − j − i − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covHookSq_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covHookSq_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":582,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L582-L597","doc":"**The second-moment anchor, Lean-locked**: `0 ≤ Cov₂(Σ_□h², ω₃)` — the ν-system's second\nmoment `Σ_v v²·ν_v` is a variance, hence nonnegative, at every level `k`. (Contrast with the\n*zeroth* moment `Σ_v ν_v = 0` and the refuted pointwise sign: the moment skeleton's exact\nconstraints survive and this one is now machine-checked.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.omegaVar_eq_centered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.omegaVar_eq_centered","kind":"theorem","line":559,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L559-L580","doc":"The variance in centered form: `Var₂(ω₃) = E₂[(ω₃ − E₂[ω₃])²]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L555-L557","doc":"The tilted weight is nonnegative (with no positivity hypothesis). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covHookSq_eq_omegaVar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covHookSq_eq_omegaVar","kind":"theorem","line":517,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L517-L553","doc":"**`Cov₂(Σ_□h², ω₃) = Var₂(ω₃)`** — the constant shift drops from the covariance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covHookSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covHookSq","kind":"def","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L513-L515","doc":"**The second moment of the ν-system**: `Cov₂(Σ_□h², ω₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookSqOmegaMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookSqOmegaMoment","kind":"def","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L507-L511","doc":"Mixed hook-square moment `E₂[Σh²·ω₃]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookSqMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hookSqMoment","kind":"def","line":502,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L502-L505","doc":"First hook-square moment `E₂[Σh²]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.omegaVar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.omegaVar","kind":"def","line":499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L499-L500","doc":"**The variance `Var₂(ω₃)`** under the Plancherel-squared weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.omegaSqMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.omegaSqMoment","kind":"def","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L495-L497","doc":"Second moment `E₂[ω₃²]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sumSqHooks_eq_omega3_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sumSqHooks_eq_omega3_add","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L482-L493","doc":"**The hook-square statistic is a constant shift of `ω₃`** on enumerated partitions:\n`Σ_□h² = ω₃ + C(k,2) + k²` — the corpus identity `Σh² = Σc² + n²` plus `Σc² = ω₃ + C(k,2)`,\nwith both shift terms constant across `partsOf k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sumSqContents_eq_contentSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.sumSqContents_eq_contentSq","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L473-L480","doc":"`IdentityI.sumSqContents` is the kernel's `contentSq` (two formalizations of the same\nnested sum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.list_sum_map_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.list_sum_map_add","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L464-L471","doc":"Finite list sums add termwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_nonpos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_nonpos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L446-L453","doc":"**Leg [A2] in hook form**: `Cov₂(ln f, ω₃) ≤ 0 ↔ 0 ≤ Cov₂(ln ∏h, ω₃)` — the anti-correlation\nof dimension with spread is exactly the *positive* correlation of total log-hook with spread. The\nopen [A2] target, restated on the hook statistic. (The pointwise-in-`s` Frullani attack on it is\nrefuted for `n ≥ 29`; the surviving routes are integral-level cancellation and the\nmoment-skeleton / even-hook-power lead.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_eq_neg_covLnHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF_eq_neg_covLnHooks","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L400-L444","doc":"**The exact hook reduction of leg [A2]**: `Cov₂(ln f, ω₃) = −Cov₂(ln ∏h, ω₃)`. The\nlog-factorial is constant on `partsOf k` (every enumerated partition sums to `k`), and covariance\nkills constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnHooks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnHooks","kind":"def","line":396,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L396-L398","doc":"**The hook–spread covariance** `Cov₂(ln ∏h, ω₃)` — the [A2] quantity in hook form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnHookOmegaMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnHookOmegaMoment","kind":"def","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L391-L394","doc":"First mixed log-hook moment `E₂[ln ∏h · ω₃]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnHookMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnHookMoment","kind":"def","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L387-L389","doc":"First log-hook moment `E₂[ln ∏h]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.log_sytDim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.log_sytDim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L368-L385","doc":"**The FRT log identity** on enumerated partitions: `ln f = ln k! − ln ∏h` — the real form of\n`numSYTenum · prodHooks = n!` through the (proved) hook-product bridge and dimension\npositivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.list_sum_map_mul_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.list_sum_map_mul_left","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L359-L366","doc":"Constants scale out of finite list sums. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.list_sum_map_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.list_sum_map_sub","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L350-L357","doc":"Finite list sums subtract termwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.deriv_tiltedMean_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.deriv_tiltedMean_zero","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L326-L329","doc":"The `deriv`-form restatement: `deriv (g k) 0 = Cov₂(ln f, ω₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tiltedMean_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tiltedMean_zero","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L304-L324","doc":"**The derivative identification (the analytic leg of the scaffold, now closed)**:\n`g′(0) = covLnF k` — the tilted mean has derivative exactly the finite-sum covariance\n`Cov₂(ln f, ω₃)` at `θ = 0`. Quotient rule on the term-by-term derivatives, with the tilted\npartition function nonvanishing by the (proved) dimension positivity. Hence `leg_A2` is\nliterally the sign of `g′(0)`, and `leg_A3` is literally the first-order Taylor-remainder\nbound: the class fields are the pincer's genuine analytic legs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tiltOmega_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tiltOmega_zero","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L294-L302","doc":"The tilted `ω₃`-sum differentiates term by term:\n`W′(0) = Σ f²·ln f·ω₃` (the `lnDimOmegaMoment` numerator). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tiltNorm_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tiltNorm_zero","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L286-L292","doc":"The tilted partition function differentiates term by term:\n`Z′(0) = Σ f²·ln f` (the `lnDimMoment` numerator). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tilt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_tilt","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L274-L284","doc":"The tilted weight is differentiable in `θ` with logarithmic derivative `ln f`:\n`(d/dθ) f^{2+θ} = f^{2+θ}·ln f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_list_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.hasDerivAt_list_sum","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L263-L272","doc":"Derivative of a finite list sum, term by term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.kernelValue_nonpos_of_legs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.kernelValue_nonpos_of_legs","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L236-L254","doc":"**The conditional kernel bound (capstone, hypothesis-free)**: the two pincer legs close the\ncovariance-kernel conjecture at level `k` — `kernelValue k ≤ 0` is *derived* from\n`KernelPincerLegs k` through the positivity of the tilted partition function (dimension\npositivity now *proved*, `YoungDiagramKernelDimPos.sytDim_pos_of_mem_partsOf`) and the `θ = 1`\nbridge. Providing the (currently absent) instance for all `k` is exactly the open problem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean_zero_of_le_twenty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean_zero_of_le_twenty","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L229-L234","doc":"**`mean_zero` is discharged for `3 ≤ k ≤ 20`** — not assumed. On this range the pincer's\npremise set reduces to the two genuinely open legs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean_zero_of_secondMomentKernel_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean_zero_of_secondMomentKernel_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L221-L227","doc":"**The mean-zero bridge**: the ℤ-form vanishing `Σ_λ (f^λ)²·ω₃(λ) = 0` gives the scaffold's\n`mean_zero` hypothesis `E₂[ω₃] = 0` outright (the quotient's numerator vanishes, so no\nnon-degeneracy of the normalisation is needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltOmega_zero_eq_secondMomentKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltOmega_zero_eq_secondMomentKernel","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L203-L219","doc":"**At `θ = 0` the tilted `ω₃`-sum IS the dim²-weighted content-spread total**:\n`W(0) = secondMomentKernel k` (cast to `ℝ`). The ℝ-side twin of\n`tiltOmega_one_eq_kernelValue`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt_zero","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L197-L201","doc":"At `θ = 0` the tilt is the plain squared dimension: `tilt 0 f = f²` (no positivity needed —\nthe exponent `0 · log f` vanishes even at `f = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltOmega_one_eq_kernelValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltOmega_one_eq_kernelValue","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L161-L180","doc":"**At `θ = 1` the tilted `ω₃`-sum IS the kernel**: `W(1) = kernelValue k` (cast to `ℝ`), since\n`f²·exp(ln f) = f³` at positive dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltNorm_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltNorm_pos","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L149-L159","doc":"The tilted partition function is positive (given the dimension positivity, which is true —\n`f^λ = #SYT ≥ 1` — and discharged list-level when the HLF divisibility bridge lands). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt_pos","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L143-L147","doc":"The tilted weight is positive at positive dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.singleRow_mem_partsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.singleRow_mem_partsOf","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L130-L141","doc":"The single-row partition `[k]` is enumerated: `partsOf k` is nonempty for `k ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean_one_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean_one_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L124-L126","doc":"**Conditional kernel sign at the tilted-mean level**: the legs force `g(1) ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.leg_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.leg_A3","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L122-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.leg_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.leg_A2","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L121-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.mean_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.mean_zero","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L120-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.KernelPincerLegs","kind":"class","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L109-L122","doc":"**The two pincer legs + the exact tilt-mean-zero identity** for level `k`. Content-bearing\n`Prop` class with **no instance** — providing an instance for all `k` IS closing the covariance\nkernel. Fields:\n\n* `mean_zero` — `g(0) = E₂[ω₃] = 0`: exact (regular-character orthogonality); ℤ-form\n  `decide`-verified `k ≤ 7` in `YoungDiagramKernel.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero_of_le_seven`.\n* `leg_A2` — `Cov₂(ln f, ω₃) ≤ 0`: the anti-correlation leg (hook/Frullani route).\n* `leg_A3` — `|g(1) − Cov₂(ln f, ω₃)| ≤ −Cov₂(ln f, ω₃)`: the remainder-domination leg (uniform\n  mixed-cumulant route; its *interpretation* as a second-order Taylor bound rides the separate\n  `g′(0) = covLnF` identification, not asserted in this file). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.pincer_arith_forces_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.pincer_arith_forces_A2","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L100-L105","doc":"The remainder domination *forces* leg [A2] arithmetically (`|·| ≥ 0` ⇒ `d ≤ 0`) — recorded so\nthe two legs' logical relationship is explicit: [A3] as stated subsumes [A2]; they remain\nseparate targets because the attack proves them by different routes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.pincer_arith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.pincer_arith","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L94-L98","doc":"**The pincer, as bare arithmetic**: if the interpolation error of `g1` against the\nfirst-order value `d` is dominated by `−d`, then `g1 ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.covLnF","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L86-L90","doc":"**The [A2] quantity**: the finite-sum covariance\n`Cov₂(ln f, ω₃) = E₂[ln f·ω₃] − E₂[ln f]·E₂[ω₃]` — the first-order response of the tilted mean,\nwhose nonpositivity is the log-dimension/content-spread anti-correlation leg. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnDimMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnDimMoment","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L82-L84","doc":"First log-dimension moment `E₂[ln f]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnDimOmegaMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lnDimOmegaMoment","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L77-L80","doc":"First mixed moment `E₂[ln f · ω₃]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltedMean","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L73-L75","doc":"The tilted mean `g(θ) = E_{2+θ}[ω₃] = W(θ)/Z(θ)` — the pincer's interpolating function.\n`g(0) = 0` exactly; the kernel sign is `g(1) ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltOmega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltOmega","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L69-L71","doc":"Tilted `ω₃`-sum `W(θ) = Σ_{λ⊢k} f^{2+θ}·ω₃(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tiltNorm","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L65-L67","doc":"Tilted partition function `Z(θ) = Σ_{λ⊢k} f^{2+θ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer.tilt","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernelPincer.lean#L61-L63","doc":"The tilted weight `f² · exp(θ·ln f)` — at `θ = 0` this is the Plancherel-squared weight `f²`;\nat `θ = 1` (for `f > 0`) it is `f³`, the kernel's weight. ","signatureChunk":0}]}